Coco Xili Tibetan antelope enters the re-emerging season - Xinhua
Xinhua News Agency, Xining, July 25 (Reporter Wang Jinjin) The reporter learned from the five beam protection stations of the Cocosili Management Office of the Yangtze River National Park of the Sanjiangyuan National Park, that the monitoring shows that the Tibetan antelopes that had previously gone to the migrating region of Zhuo Nai Lake in the hinterland of Cocosiri are gradually ending the litter and starting to return to their original habitat with the cubs.
According to the surveillance screen near the protection station, on July 25, about 40 female Tibetan antelopes led three Tibetan antelope cubs through the Qinghai-Tibet highway 3002 kilometers, the Qinghai-Tibetan railway five girder north bridge, the Tibetan antelope has begun to move back.
According to expert analysis, in recent years, the Tibetan antelope cubs in the returning sheep have accounted for one-fourth to one-fifth of the overall number.
Lian Xinming, an associate researcher at the Northwest Plateau Biological Research Institute of the Chinese Academy of Sciences, said: “In the early stage of the relocation, Tibetan antelopes face a higher risk of predation, so the number of cubs in the flock will be relatively small, and there may even be no pups.”
According to Sanjiangyuan National Park Management Office of the Yangtze River Source Park, the overall number of Tibetan antelope relocation is increasing year by year, and the number of Tibetan antelope relocations in 2019 was 4,860, an increase of 338 compared with 2018.
“It is expected that this year’s Tibetan antelope relocation will end at the beginning of September, and it is still expected to continue to increase.”
Tibetan antelopes protect animals at the national level.
At the end of May of each year, Tibetan antelopes from Sanjiangyuan in Qinghai, Qiantang in Tibet, and Aljin Mountain in Xinjiang are required to go to Lake Chonai, which is located in the hinterland of Cocosiri.
Wu Xiaomin, a conservation expert for Tibetan antelopes in China and a researcher at the Shaanxi Provincial Animal Research Institute (Northwest Endangered Animal Research Institute), said: "Tibetan antelope's relocating is the process of returning to its habitat with the cubs after the end of the litter. At first, the relocating group that left the litter is relatively large, but then the Tibetan antelope will return to their respective habitats according to different geographical populations and different paths."
In order to ensure the safe relocation of the Tibetan sheep, the reporter learned that a few days ago, Sanjiangyuan National Park Yangtze National Park Cocosiri Management Office has arranged for staff to continue to carry out video monitoring and district patrols in the main relocation area.
If it is found that there are Tibetan sheep trying to cross the road, the mountain patrol team will carry out temporary traffic control at the first time, so that the sheep can safely pass through the wildlife channel, so as to ensure that they will not be interfered with by humans as much as possible on the return journey.
So, how to relieve the heat in daily life?
According to experts, it is best not to walk or work in the scorching sun before and after noon as much as possible, because the sunshine during this period is the strongest, and the possibility of heat stroke is higher.
If you have to go out at this time, you must do a good job of protection, such as wearing umbrellas, wearing sun hats, wearing sunglasses, it is best to apply sunscreen with conditions to prevent sunburn.
The clothes try to use light-colored, well-breathed cotton, hemp, silk texture, less chemical fiber clothing, so as to avoid a lot of sweating can not timely heat dissipation, causing heat stroke.
In the hot and sweltering weather, it is necessary to prepare a sufficient amount of water to drink, drink in time, do not wait until you are thirsty to drink water, because once the feeling of thirst indicates that the body has a lack of water, each drink water is controlled at 150 ml to 200 ml, drink warm boiling water, do not drink iced water.
According to the temperature, the average person drinks 1.5 to 2 liters of water per day, and high-temperature workers drink 3 to 5 liters of water per day.
When sweating more, some salt water can be appropriately supplemented to make up for the salt lost by the human body due to sweating.
In addition, in the summer, the human body is prone to a lack of potassium, which makes people feel tired and tired, and the potassium tea is an excellent cooling drink.
In the summer, eat fruits and vegetables with high moisture content, such as lettuces, cucumbers, tomatoes, etc.; fresh fruits, such as peaches, apricots, watermelons, melon and other moisture content of 80% to 90%, can be used to add water; dairy products can not only replenish water, but also can meet the nutritional needs of the body.
In addition, people who work in a high temperature environment should properly supplement drinks containing elements such as potassium and magnesium.
In the summer, the days and nights are short, the temperature is high, the human body's metabolism is strong, the consumption is also large, and it is easy to feel tired.
Adequate sleep can relax the brain and various systems of the body, which is conducive to work and study, and is also a measure to prevent heat stroke.
According to experts, the best time to go to bed is from 22:00 to 23:00, and the best time to get up is from 5:30 to 6:30.
Be careful not to lie under air-conditioning outlets and electric fans during sleep, so as not to suffer from air-conditioning diseases and thermal injuries.
Experts suggest that in outdoor activities or high-temperature work, you can carry ten drops of water, dandelion, aromatic water or chrysanthemum pills and other anti-heat drugs, or placed in the nearby workplace, ready to use, in order to prevent the occurrence of heat stroke.
Graduate art exhibition moved into the shopping mall public welfare exhibition-Xinhua.com
In the "cloud graduation" season of major colleges and universities, a rare offline graduate art exhibition opened warmly over the weekend.
However, it is neither in the art museum, nor on the campus, but appears in the public space of Chaoyang Grand Hyatt, which will be open to the public free of charge until August 23.
The reporter learned that this 2020 graduate art exhibition collected 50 pieces/group works of 57 young artists from the Central Academy of Fine Arts, the Communication University of China and the Tianjin Academy of Fine Arts, the exhibition space was extended from the 2nd floor to the 6th floor, and made full use of the light boxes in the building for the display of graphic works to maximize the artistic atmosphere of the graduation season.
Under the epidemic, the significance of this exhibition is particularly special.
Chaoyang Yuecheng Mei Chen head Ge Pingping said: "We chose to go to the 'cloud' graduation exhibition to bring back to the offline space again, but also hope to let more people see young people's own exploration and understanding of the world, amplify the healing power of the arts for society and the mind."
She revealed that the works of the exhibition were collected from the graduates of several major art colleges and universities, and they were selected to be suitable for commercial space display, and the form of the works from the traditional shelf paintings and sculptures, to new media installations, interactive animations, VR panoramas, the volume and richness are the highest in the past few years.
Among them, Li Yunxiao expressed his feelings in this epidemic through a mixture of mechanical and manual creative language in the "first battle of 2020"; Liu Jiaying explored the themes of "cryptocurrency", "credit creation", "transactions" and other themes through the works created on the Ethereum blockchain; Zhang Jiaqi's "cat forest" and Qiu Daqiang's "hook" are often accompanied by human beings.
Among the few self-exhibited graduates, there is Li Jingyin from the Sculpture Department of the Tianjin Academy of Fine Arts.
"I came to Beijing on July 7, I was actually a little worried about the epidemic, and I did the nucleic acid test three days in advance, which was released with alcohol cotton and test reports."
The structure of his "Yesterday as a mystery" is more complicated, and he has to do it personally.
At the same time, he also undertakes the task of helping his classmates to repair damaged works.
â€œThe exhibition was held at 4:30 a.m., and then the repair, the time was very tight, I forgot to take a picture with the work, and it was a bit of a pity."
He hopes that when the epidemic is more stabilised, he and his classmates will come to Beijing to see his works exhibition.
(Reporter Li Jun)
That morning, the 65-year-old Bolsonaro posted a photo on Twitter, wearing sneakers, not wearing a mask, sitting in front of a table for breakfast with a smile on his face, a thumbs-up in one hand and a box of hydroxychloroquine in the other.
He tweeted: "Good morning everyone, the new coronavirus test result: negative."
However, Bolsonaro did not say when the negative test for the new coronavirus was carried out.
On July 5, Bolsonaro showed symptoms of new crown pneumonia, tested positive for the virus on the 6th, and on the 7th, he claimed to be diagnosed with new crown pneumonia through live television.
On the 14th and the 21st, Bolsonaro was tested for the new coronavirus twice, and the results were still positive.
During the isolation period, Bolsonaro repeatedly showed the hydroxychloroquine drug he was taking through social media, and said that hydroxychloroquine has a good effect on the new crown pneumonia, it feels very good after taking it, and its good physical condition is due to hydroxychloroquine, arguing that Brazilian medical institutions use hydroxychloroquine drugs to treat new crown pneumonia.
According to Brazilian media reports, as of now, there are also five cabinet ministers and 10 governors in Brazil who have been diagnosed with new crown pneumonia.
A small plane crashed in the Swiss Alps, killing all four people on board.
According to the European Network quoted by the European Union News Agency, on July 25 local time, the Swiss police reported to the media that a small aircraft crashed in the Swiss Alps on the 25th.
The two Swiss and the two Austrians were killed in the accident.
According to reports, police in the southern Swiss state of Wallis said that a small plane crashed more than 3,000 meters above sea level near the peaks of the Valais Alps, and rescuers rushed to the scene of the crash and confirmed that all the four people on the plane were killed.
Valais state police said that witnesses called police at 12:25 p.m. on the 25th and said that he had witnessed a small plane falling from the sky.
A few minutes later, the witness again informed the police that there was heavy smoke at the crash site.
After the police received the alarm, they quickly coordinated the fire officers, medical staff and rescue personnel and took a helicopter to the scene of the accident.
After rescuers arrived at the crash site, they found that all four people on board had been killed.
According to police, the victims of the accident included two Swiss nationals, aged 50 and 66, and two Austrians, aged 46 and 50.
Police are currently working with the Swiss Transport Safety Investigation Board to investigate the cause of the crash.
Heavy rains occur in 33 districts and counties in Chongqing, issuing yellow and orange flood warnings
Zhongxin Network Chongqing, July 26 (Reporter Liu Xianglin) The reporter learned from the Chongqing Municipal Water Conservancy Bureau on the 26th that in the past 24 hours, there have been heavy rains in 33 districts and counties in Chongqing, of which heavy rains have occurred in 16 districts and counties.
The heavy rain caused 71 small and medium-sized rivers in Chongqing to rise, and two flood warnings have been issued.
According to the Chongqing Hydrological Monitoring Station, from 8 o'clock on the 25th to 8 o'clock on the 26th, there were heavy rains in most parts of Chongqing.
Thirteen rainstorms occurred in 33 districts and prefectures, such as Zhongxian, Kaizhou and Wuxi; the maximum daily rainfall appeared in Longshan Village, Nanchuan Jinshan Town, at 19.75 mm.
71 small and medium-sized rivers, such as Tongnan River, Qiongjiang and Kaizhou South River, have 1 to 7 meters of rising water, and the highest water level does not exceed the alert water level.
It is estimated that from 8 o'clock on the 26th to 8 o’clock on the 27th, small and medium-sized rivers in most parts of Chongqing may have different degrees of rising water processes, and some small and medium-sized rivers may have super-police level floods.
It will also pay attention to possible transit floods in the Yangtze and Jialing rivers.
