Reward of 50,000 yuan Hubei Enshi praised the sand dam landslide "early warning the first person"-Zhongxin.com
Hubei Daily News (Reporter Linjing) On July 26, Enshi City commended Chen Guangming, a geo-disaster point monitor who made an important contribution to sand dam landslide early warning, and sent him a bonus of 50,000 yuan.
At the same time, the city's party members and cadres are called upon to learn the spirit of his dedication, courage, initiative and dedication.
On July 21, the sand dam occurred in the sand dams of Tanbao Township of Enshi City, which led to the formation of a barrier lake in the dry river of the Qing River, and Chen Guangming, 58, was the first person to give early warning of the landslide.
On the afternoon of July 17, Chen Guangming learned that the walls of the villagers' homes were cracked, and immediately went to the scene to check.
He had just walked five or six hundred meters out of his home, and he could see that the village road cracked four or five centimeters, along the road all the way to the cornfield, with a length of about 50 meters.
Chen was alert and sent the photos of the cracking of the highway to the "geological disaster monitor contact group" in the township for the first time.
After on-the-spot inspection and judgment by the relevant person in charge of the Tunbao Township Natural Planning Institute, there is a great possibility of a landslide, and a decision to vacate the masses is immediately made.
Chen Guangming's timely early warning obtained 36 hours of valuable time for the safe evacuation of 1,339 people in 315 households in the area.
In this major geological disaster, there were no casualties.
Chen Guangming's serious and responsible professionalism was praised by the masses.
In the face of praise, he said: "There is no one to save, it's my responsibility."
The University of Australia to develop a new drug is expected to be used to treat blood vessel blockage caused by the new crown
SYDNEY, July 26 (Xinhua) -- researchers at Monash University in Australia are working on a new drug that could help prevent heart disease and stroke, and hope that the drug could be used to treat blood vessel blockage caused by the new coronavirus.
The researchers found that an enzyme in platelets accelerates platelet clotting prior to a heart attack or stroke.
As a result, they developed a drug that can temporarily suppress platelet coagulation, so as to avoid vascular blockage and play a preventive role in heart disease and stroke.
The researchers said that the drug will only inhibit the clotting effect of platelets in the event of signs of heart attack or stroke.
Because studies have shown that similar vascular blockage is one of the leading causes of death in patients with new coronary diseases, the researchers hope that the drug can be used for the treatment of such severe patients in the future.
At present, the drug has achieved good results in animal model experiments, and the researchers are preparing for the next stage of human clinical trials.
The research results have recently been published in the American Journal of Science and Translational Medicine.
