During the viewing period, spectators are required to wear a mask throughout the process, take a seat on the number, and strictly stay one meter apart.
When exiting, the spectator must maintain the "one-meter line" social distance in an orderly manner in accordance with the order from then forward, first on both sides and in the middle.
Xinjiang deeply cultivates "sunflower fields" to make good use of clean energy
2020-07-26 15:43:42 Source: China News Network Author: Chen Haifeng Responsibility Editor: Chen Haifeng
Xinhua News Agency Xinjiang Hami July 26 topic: Xinjiang deep plow "Sunflower field" to make good use of clean energy
There are more than 6,000 pentagonal heliostats, each 48 square meters, arranged neatly in a circle, such as a silver "sunflower field", rotating with the sun, reflecting the sunlight to the center more than 200 meters high heat-absorbing tower to achieve power generation.
On the 25th, the reporter saw this scene at the China Electric Power Project Hami molten molten salt tower solar-thermal power plant in Yiwu Lake Town, Hami City, Xinjiang.
"The so-called molten-salt tower-type solar-thermal power generation is the reflection of sunlight through the mirror to the heat-absorbing tower to form thermal energy, and then through the traditional power generation technology to convert thermal energy into electrical energy."
Zhang Yong, deputy general manager of CMC Hami Solar Thermal Power Generation Co., Ltd., said that its design principle is similar to the solar cooker used in the rural areas of northwestern China.
The power plant started construction in October 2017 and was grid-connected by the end of last year, covering an area of 6,600 acres, with a total plan to install 14,500 heliostats.
"Compared to the traditional solar power generation technology, its biggest advantage is that the aggregated thermal energy can be stored, and it can also generate electricity at night."
Zhang Yong said that the 13-hour heat storage system configured by the project can maintain continuous and stable operation of the generator set, which is not affected by changes in lighting; it can also quickly participate in the peaking of the power grid according to the needs of the power grid.
After the project is completely completed, it can achieve an annual power generation of 198 million degrees, save more than 60,000 tons of standard coal per year, reduce more than 60 tons of sulphur dioxide, more than 60 tons of nitrogen oxides, about 20 tons of soot, and more than 150,000 tons of carbon dioxide, providing a steady stream of clean energy for the local area.
In addition, there is another piece of silver "sunflower field" in Hami Shicheng Photovoltaic Industrial Park.
The Hamifu solar photovoltaic power station covers an area of more than 2,300 acres, and the 714 power generation equipment that has been built has also followed the rotation of the sun, always maintaining a 90-degree right angle between the sun and the concentrator surface.
“We use bi-axis-tracked concentrated power generation technology, and through unified and integrated control, all power generation equipment will adjust the angle according to the height of the sun to maintain power generation efficiency.”
Duan Mengqi, director of the power station, said that under good lighting weather conditions, the power generation technology can be increased by about 20% compared with traditional photovoltaic power generation efficiency.
In the first half of this year, the power station has achieved more than 7 million degrees of power generation, complementing the local electricity demand.
Shichengzi Photovoltaic Industrial Park is the largest photovoltaic industrial demonstration park with the most complete type of photovoltaic modules in Xinjiang, with a total of 38 photovoltaic power generation projects, with a total installed capacity of 820,000 kilowatts.
In the first half of this year, the completed power generation exceeded 110 million degrees, an increase of 6% over the same period in 2019.
Hamid is one of the regions with the best solar resource conditions in China.
The average annual total solar radiance is more than 6,200 per square meter, and the number of sunshine hours per year is about 3,200 hours.
In recent years, the city has made great efforts to develop the photovoltaic industry and planted "sunflower fields".
In the first half of this year, the city's photovoltaic power generation has exceeded 1.4 billion degrees, an increase of about 14% year-on-year.
At present, there are more than 330 grid-connected photovoltaic power plants in Xinjiang with an installed capacity of more than 10 million kilowatts.
It is expected that the annual photovoltaic power generation will reach 15 billion degrees this year, which can replace more than 6 million tons of standard coal.
The police informed that the details of "female university students to travel to Qinghai lost contact" search and rescue work continues - Xinhua
Xinhua News Agency, Xining, July 26 (Reporter Wang Jinjin Zhou Zhe) Recently, "a female college student lost contact after a trip to Qinghai Geermu" attracted the attention of netizens.
On the 26th, the Public Security Bureau of Golmud City, a Mongolian and Tibetan Autonomous Prefecture in Qinghai Province, reported on the 26th that Huang, a student at a university in Nanjing, is still in a state of missing contact, and the police in many places are going deep along the lost ground in Huang to actively carry out looking for work.
On July 10, 2020, the public security detachment of the Public Security Detachment of the Gemu City Public Security Bureau of Haixi Prefecture received a notice from its superior that Huang, a student of a university in Nanjing, took the Z164 train from Nanjing to Golmud on the 5th of July, and on July 9, it lost the machine in the south-western area of Qingshui River in Qumalai Prefecture, Yushu Tibetan Autonomous Prefecture, Qinghai Province.
According to Golmud City Public Security Bureau's investigation situation, Huang entered the territory of Qinghai Province at 19:54 on July 6, and arrived in Golmud City at 4 o'clock on the 7th.
At 8 o'clock on the same day, the disembarked personnel Huang took a taxi from Golmud Grand Hotel towards the G109 national highway, and arrived at the Cocosiri Sonandaj protection station at 12 o'clock at 12 o'clock, the taxi driver returned alone, and Huang arrived in the Qingshui River area near the Sonam Daj protection station at 15:00 on the 9th until 18 o'clock on the 9th to shut down in the area.
In the further investigation, the police found that Huang had passed through the Najigou checkpoint at 17:07 on July 13.
The Najigou checkpoint is a checkpoint set up by Naqu City in the Tibet Autonomous Region in the Nanshankou of Golmud City, because there is no video surveillance of the checkpoint, it is not possible to identify myself and the vehicle information, the police can only drive along the way to find, and coordinate the checkpoints along the Tibetan coast if Huang Moumou is found, immediately get in touch with the Golmud City Public Security Bureau.
According to the latest situation, at 1 a.m. on July 26, the Golmud City Public Security Bureau organized rescue forces to carry rescue equipment, and went to the unfrozen spring protection station along the Qinghai-Tibetan highway to search, and actively contacted the Sichuan police, the Tibetan police and the Nanjing police to work together.
The local police hope that the majority of netizens and all sectors of the society, if there are relevant clues, will be provided in a timely manner to the Golmud police and the Nanjing Jiangning police, and strive to find the missing person at an early date.
At the same time, the relevant experts suggest that tourists should be standardized, rational and civilized in outdoor activities, pay attention to roadside warning signs at any time, do not venture into no-man's land, encounter unexpected situations, and call the police in a timely manner.
The U.S. media uncovers the fact that the U.S. unwarranted demand that China close the Consulate General in Houston
2020-07-26 14:40:44 Source: CCTV Author: Zhu Yanjing Responsibility Editor: Zhu Yanjing
The U.S. media has revealed the fact that the U.S. unwarranted demand that China close the Consulate General in Houston.
On the 24th, the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs notified the U.S. Embassy in China that the Chinese side decided to revoke the license for the establishment and operation of the U.S. Consulate General in Chengdu, and put forward specific requirements for the suspension of all operations and activities of the Consulate General of the United States on the 21st, in response to the U.
The U.S. government's behavior has aroused a lot of attention, and its political motives have been questioned by foreign media and scholars.
Why do you want China to close the Consulate General?
A number of foreign media said that it is not clear why the United States will choose the Chinese Consulate General in Houston, but for the purpose of this move, foreign media bluntly said: for the election.
CNN reported on the 23rd that the U.S. government's call for China's closure of the Consulate General in Houston raised the public's doubts about its political motives.
The US government's disastrous response to the new crown epidemic has caused President Donald Trump's poor poll support before the election.
White House officials have privately said that the hard-line strategy against China is aimed at rescuing Trump’s approval rating, as well as diverting responsibility for the failure of the White House’s response to the outbreak.
China’s Consulate General in Houston is a “politics-driven, very cautious” U.S.-choice target that the U.S. government has chosen “to create a tough attitude while avoiding the risk of significant conflict.”
The British Broadcasting Corporation (BBC) also believes that at a time when the U.S. general election season is approaching and the U.S. economy has been hit hard by the epidemic, Trump believes that "playing the 'China card' has a political advantage."
The current situation is a “spiraning, tit-for-tat struggle,” driven in part by the U.S. government from the perspective of domestic considerations, and will only worsen tensions between China and the United States.
CBS reported that Trump's re-election prospects are under pressure due to the outbreak, and he has repeatedly blamed China because of the outbreak.
The United States makes almost daily new actions in response to Trump’s so-called “Chinese exploitation of the United States.”
"The Consulate General of Houston is very important in establishing relations between the two countries."
U.S. demands that China close its consulate in Houston have heightened tensions between the world’s two largest economies.
If the Chinese Consulate General in Houston is closed, in addition to the diplomatic influence, Chinese citizens in the southern United States face difficulties in obtaining consular services, and U.S. citizens seeking visas and other services also face difficulties.
A U.S.-based business group lamented the U.S. demand that China close its consulate in Houston, saying it played an important role in establishing trade, investment and cultural ties between the two countries.
The Associated Press believes that this reflects the importance of China's economy.
The U.S. "Foreign Policy magazine website believes that the U.S. move "is part of a series of provocative measures that will only worsen U.S.-China relations."
Jonathan Pollack, an expert on East Asia at the Brookings Institution, a U.S. think tank, said that since the United States and China established full diplomatic relations in 1979, he can't think of any action that can be compared with the U.S. action against the Chinese Consulate General in Houston.
Hong Kong's "South China Morning Post" reported that this move by the United States is unprecedented in more than 40 years of diplomatic relations between the two countries.
Analysts believe that such a move may cause lasting damage.
The Chinese Consulate General in Houston was built in 1979 and is the first Chinese Consulate General in the United States.
At present, China has an embassy and five consulates-general in the United States.
Russia holds military parade to celebrate Navy Day - Xinhua
On July 26, in St. Petersburg, Russia, the ships lined up to participate in Navy Day celebrations.
Xinhua News Agency (photo by Mojina)
MOSCOW, July 26 (Xinhua) -- Russia's various fleets held a military parade on the 26th to commemorate the 324th anniversary of the founding of the Russian Navy.
On the same day, Russia's North Sea, the Baltic Sea, the Black Sea, the Caspian Sea and the Pacific Fleet held a military parade in the waters of their respective bases, with a total of 15,000 soldiers, 219 ships of various types, and 71 military aircraft participating.
The Russian president and supreme commander of the armed forces, Vladimir Putin, attended the military parade of the Baltic Fleet.
More than 4000 military personnel, 46 ships and more than 40 fighters participated in the local military parade.
Putin first inspected the ships in the waters of the naval base in Kronstadt in the Baltic Sea.
After that, he reached the waters of the Neva River in the center of St. Petersburg in a speedboat and went ashore to watch the military parade held on the Neva River.
Speaking at the military parade, Putin said that the technical level of modernization of the Russian Navy's equipment has been continuously improved in recent years, and the Russian Navy will receive a total of about 40 new ships equipped with a unique hypersonic strike system in 2020.
In addition, the commander-in-chief of the Russian Navy Yevmenov recently said in an interview with the Russian Ministry of Defense's "Red Star" that Russia's plan to build ships has been effectively implemented, and the number of new ships planned to be received by the Russian Navy in 2020 is a relatively large scale in recent years.
In 1696, Tsar Peter the Great initiated the formation of a maritime fleet, which began the history of the Russian Navy.
The last Sunday in July every year is the Day of the Russian Navy.
