The longest high-speed high-speed rail tunnel in the Three Gorges Reservoir area - Sino-New Network
2020-07-26 17:34:48 Source: China News Network Author: Chen Haifeng Responsibility Editor: Chen Haifeng
It is the construction site of the Little Three Gorges Tunnel.
China Railway Chengdu Bureau Group Co., Ltd.
Zhongxin Network Chongqing July 26 (Reporter Han Lu) The reporter was informed on the 26th from the China Railway Chengdu Bureau Group Co., Ltd., with a total length of about 18.9 kilometers.
It is understood that the Little Three Gorges Tunnel is not only the longest high-speed rail tunnel in the Three Gorges Reservoir area, but also the longest single-hole two-line high-speed rail tunnel with a design speed of 350 km/h under construction.
Zhengwan high-speed rail is located in Henan, Hubei and Chongqing three provinces and cities, in Zhengzhou north of Beijing-Guangzhou, Xulan high-speed rail arrived in Chongqing, is an important part of China's "eight vertical and eight horizontal" high-speed railway network along the river channel and Hunan channel.
Zhengwan high-speed high-speed rail Little Three Gorges Tunnel opened the whole line on the 26th.
It runs through the scene.
Zhengwan high-speed rail starts in Zhengzhou City, Henan Province, south-west through Pingdingshan City, Nanyang City, Hubei Province Xiangyang City to Chongqing Wanzhou District, the total length is about 818 kilometers, the design speed is 350 km/h, Chongqing territory of about 184 kilometers.
Among them, the section from Zhengzhou to Xiangyang has been opened on December 1, 2019, and the Chongqing section is stepping up construction.
On the 26th, the small Three Gorges Tunnel was a full-line control project of the Zhengwan high-speed railway, and the project was located at the border between Fengjie County and Wushan County in Chongqing, with a total length of about 18.9 kilometers and a maximum burial depth of 890 meters.
The construction of the tunnel began in February 2017 and was completed on July 26, 2020.
According to Wang Jun, the head of the design of the Zhengwan high-speed rail tunnel of Zhengwan High-speed Railway Engineering Group Co., Ltd., the geological conditions in the location of the small Three Gorges Tunnel are very complicated, facing risks such as karst, surmount water, and soft rock deformation, which belongs to Class I high-risk tunnels, and the tunnel design and construction are extremely difficult.
"In the process of project construction, we adopted advanced geological forecasts such as geological survey methods, material exploration and advanced drilling methods, and adopted a special design scheme for more than 30 caves of various types. For example, a 24-meter-long bridge has been designed and built, spanning large caves with a longitudinal length of more than 10 meters and a depth of more than 55 meters to avoid tunnel subsidence," the royal army said.
According to the China Railway Tunnel Bureau of the construction side of the construction of the tunnel, the combination of dredging and blocking, through the construction of cross-hole flat guides, slurry blocking water, strengthening tunnel structural support and the construction of sewage treatment stations, not only to ensure the orderly progress of the project, but also to avoid the construction and drainage of the small Three Gorges Scenic area of the water damage, while successfully overcoming up to 7 kilometers of soft rock deformation and other bad geology, the maximum daily inflow of water up to 157,000 cubic meters.
After the Zhengwan high-speed rail line is completed, it will become a new convenient and fast passenger main channel to the Central Plains, northern China and the northeast region in the southwestern region of China, which is of great significance to improving the capacity and quality of north-eastern railway lanes in the southwestern region, improving the layout of the regional road network, accelerating the development and urbanization of tourism resources along the route, promoting regional coordinated development, and promoting the implementation of the western development strategy.
Experts say it's unconstitutional to gather immigration data for House seat allocation through U.S. Census
Some civil rights groups and several U.S. cities and counties have sued the U.S. federal government, saying Trump’s presidential palace’s attempt to exclude undocumented immigrants from the U.S. census is unworkable and unconstitutional.
The U.S. Census will determine the allocation of seats in the U.S. House of Representatives.
Sarah Brannon, an executive lawyer for the American Civil Liberties Union, told VOA that “it doesn’t work to do that.”
She went on to say that it would be difficult and “not very reliable” for Trump’s request to determine the citizenship of the person receiving the census in the census.
A lawsuit was filed Thursday against Trump’s executive order.
A number of cities in New Jersey and the state of Georgia have joined the lawsuit.
Arlington County of Virginia also joined the lawsuit on Friday.
“The U.S. Constitution calls for an accurate inventory of our population every 10 years. We have to have an accurate inventory of everyone living in Arlington County and not allow this illegal attempt to frighten and reduce the size of our immigrant communities.”
Other organizations and individuals praised President Donald Trump’s executive order.
Alabama Attorney General Marshall described the order as a “victory” for the state.
He stated that “the allocation of seats in the House of Representatives of the Länder and in the Electoral College must be based on the number of residents living in the states and the number of residents legally residing”.
The U.S. Supreme Court last year blocked the Trump administration’s inclusion of the citizenship issue in its 2020 census form.
Earlier this week, President Donald Trump signed an executive order directing Commerce Secretary Wilbur Ross of the U.S. Census Bureau to submit data on the unlicensed population obtained by the U.S. Census, so that the administration can exclude those unlicensed populations from state census numbers and determine whether each state is increasing or reducing or maintaining House seats.
The U.S. reassigns seats in the House every 10 years based on demographic changes.
Chongqing's 33 districts and counties torrential rain local launch of flood control level IV emergency response-Zhongxin.com
Xinhua News Agency, Chongqing, July 26 (Reporter Ke Gaoyang, Li Song) The reporter learned from the flood control and drought relief headquarters in Chongqing that Chongqing has ushered in a new round of heavy rainfall weather process since July 25th, 33 districts and counties have dropped heavy rains, 4 small and medium-sized rivers have super-alert water level floods, and the local flood control level IV has been launched.
According to the hydrological monitoring station in Chongqing, from 8 o'clock on the 25th to 8 o'clock on the 26th, most parts of Chongqing ushered in heavy rains, and heavy rains occurred in 33 districts and counties such as Jiangjin, Qijiang and Wulong, among which 16 districts and counties such as Wanzhou, Yunyang and Nanchuan experienced heavy rainfall.
The maximum daily rainfall occurred in Longshan Village, Jinshan Town, Nanchuan, at 197.5 millimeters.
Affected by heavy rainfall, four small and medium-sized rivers of Donkey Creek in Jiangjin District, Yingyang River in Fuling District, Yingyang River in Kaizhou District and Gongtan River in Yunyang County experienced super-alert water level floods, and the current water level is still rising.
The heavy rainfall has also led to a landslide in Liujing Village, the land township of Wulong District, resulting in the interruption of village road road traffic, and the slippery slope into the Wujiang tributary along the Cang River, blocking the river to form a dyke lake, the local government has urgently organized the transfer of the downstream masses.
In response to the heavy rains, the flood control and drought relief headquarters in Chongqing issued the river flood level III early warning information at 13 o'clock on the 26th, and launched flood control level IV emergency response, requiring the relevant districts, counties and units to strengthen inspection and watch, timely mobilize emergency rescue teams and materials, and evacuate and transfer the people in threatened areas.
