Tunisian president nominates new prime minister
Xinhua News Agency, Tunisia, July 25 (Reporter Huang Ling) Tunisia's presidential office issued a notice on the 25th, saying that on the same day, President Saeed nominated the caretaker government's Interior Minister Hisham Mehisi as the new prime minister.
In accordance with the constitution, Mehsch should complete the formation of the government within one month and submit the list of the formation of the new government to the parliament for approval.
The composition of the new government must be approved by more than half of the 217 members of parliament.
