Various departments actively implement flood control measures to ensure transportation safety
BEIJING, July 26 (Xinhua) -- Since the beginning of the summer, many parts of our country have been hit by heavy rainfall.
In order to do a good job in flood prevention and transportation safety, all departments stick to their posts, strengthen the investigation and remediation of hidden dangers, strengthen emergency response, and fully implement various flood control measures.
According to the latest statistics from the China National Railway Group Co., Ltd., the railway department has dispatched more than 280,000 inspection personnel, investigated more than 90,000 bridges, more than 17,000 tunnels, and more than 240,000 culverts.
Since July 1, the country's major railway trunk lines and freight lanes have remained safe and unimpeded, and the overall transportation order has been in good order, and the direct passenger train departure, operation and arrival rate has reached 97.7%, 87.1% and 86.8% respectively.
China Railway Nanchang Bureau Group Co., Ltd. dispatch office to strengthen emergency response, the designated person is responsible for dynamic tracking and grasp of flood control tools, road material reserves and storage, in the event of sudden disaster failure, rapid notification of information, start emergency response.
Recently, in the face of heavy rainfall, which led to the security threat caused by heavy rainfall on the Yiwan Railway Qingjiang Bridge, the professional and technical personnel of China Railway Wuhan Bureau Group Co., Ltd. organized professional and technical personnel to monitor the Qingjiang Bridge for 24 hours, and established an all-weather communication mechanism with the local emergency department to grasp and deal with dangerous hazards in a timely manner.
In order to ensure the safety of summer transportation and electricity consumption, the power supply company of the state-of-the-art network, combined with the climatic characteristics of the flood season, worked closely with the local meteorological and railway departments to strengthen the inspection of railway power supply lines and facilities and equipment in the jurisdiction, and strengthened the emergency treatment of landslides, landslides, mudslides and other related accidents in line corridors.
In order to further do a good job in flood prevention and control, Oriental Aviation Technology Co., Ltd. set up an emergency rescue reserve team to carry out flood control and disaster prevention knowledge training, and formulate flight plans according to the daily weather and typhoon and other early warning conditions, and do a good job in the preparation for the operation and recovery of parked aircraft in coastal areas.
