U.S. White House adviser "anti-bite" states to return to work too early
U.S. White House adviser "anti-bite" the states to return to work too early
According to local time on July 23, the number of confirmed cases of new crown pneumonia in the United States exceeded 4 million, accounting for 30% of global cases.
Over the past few months, U.S. President Donald Trump has repeatedly asked the states of the country to return to school, until recently to change their attitude and take the initiative to wear masks in public, and his advisers have "taken a bite" that it is too early for some state governments to return to work.
On the 22nd, White House presidential adviser Kellyanne Conway said at a press conference that some state governments did not comply with return-to-work standards and restarted places such as bars prematurely.
Conway also mentioned that previous statements that the president has "absolute power" to determine the return to work of the states are false rumors.
“The president is a federalist, and he believes the states have autonomy.”
She defended Trump.
However, Conway's "discussions" were personally uttered by Trump at the White House epidemic briefing on April 13.
This self-satisfying operation was ridiculed by netizens as "rewriting history".
Kellyanne Conway wants to rewrite history, she’s a liar.
Trump called Michigan Gov. Gretchen Whitmer a dictator because she followed medical guidelines and insisted on a shutdown.
Trump wants to push for a return to work so he can hold a rally.
This isn’t the first time Kellyanne Conway has caused controversy.
In an interview with Fox News on April 15, Conway blurted out, “It’s COVID-19 and it’s not COVID-1, my friends!”
She seems to understand the "19" as a version number, by the netizens frantically ridiculed: no common sense to look at the newspaper!
The three-year-old's college playground was smashed to play, and was it right to complain to the school after being compensated?
2020-07-26 05:01:11 Source:Legal Daily Author:Wang Sisuo Responsibility Editor:Wang Sixuo
The playground was smashed, and the children were compensated and then sued the school.
□ Zhao Yifan, Correspondent
Three-year-old Xiao Wen was playing in a university playground when he was accidentally smashed in the head by the softball team's Chen during the pitch.
After Chen's compensation, Xiao Wen's father, Mr. Wen, took the school to the court as Xiaowen's legal representative, demanded an apology from the school where the incident occurred, and paid a total of 20,000 yuan for medical expenses and moral damage soothing.
Recently, the Beijing Haidian District People's Court after the hearing of the case that the school set up a protective network on the playground at the time of the incident, has fulfilled its appropriate safety and security obligations, and Chen has paid compensation, according to which the judgment rejected the plaintiff's lawsuit.
Mr. Wen claimed that during the summer vacation of 2019, he took Xiaowen to play in the school playground, when the softball team was training in the playground.
In order to avoid the resulting risks, Xiao Wen, Mr. Wen and a large number of other children and parents are active in the safe area designated by the softball team.
However, after the softball team player Chen left his hand while pitching, causing the softball to fly across the grid to the above-mentioned safe area and hit the back of the small text.
Mr. Wen immediately took Xiaowen to the hospital for medical treatment and was diagnosed with a head injury.
Mr. Wen believes that the facilities in the school stadium do not meet the relevant safety regulations and do not effectively manage the team and related facilities.
The school's negligence has led to the above-mentioned incidents, resulting in great physical and mental suffering, and at the same time, it has brought great suffering to his family, for which the school should bear legal responsibility.
In this regard, the school argued that the school has set up a protective network in the playground, and posted management regulations and training notices, informing them to keep a safe distance from the training ground and remind them to pay attention to their own safety, and the plaintiff could not prove that the school did not fulfill its safety and security obligations, so it did not agree to compensation.
After the court hearing, it was found that the venue involved in the incident was a free and open venue for the university to the public, although the school had a safety and security obligation in the management of the playground, but this safety and security obligation only needs to meet the general duty of care.
At the time of the incident, the school had set up a protective network in the playground and had fulfilled its appropriate safety and security obligations, and Chen also compensated Xiao Wen for medical expenses, transportation expenses and other losses of more than two thousand yuan in accordance with the previous compensation agreement, and the two sides agreed on a one-time settlement of the dispute.
Later, Xiao Wen's parents once again claimed the school's compensation, and there was no basis, and the court's judgment rejected all the plaintiff's claims.
Both parties did not appeal after the verdict, which is now in force.
According to Article 37 of China's tort liability law, the school, as the manager of a public place, has the obligation of safety and security; in the case of damage caused by the third party's behavior of others, the third party shall bear the tort liability, and the manager of the public place who fails to meet the safety and security obligations shall bear the corresponding supplementary responsibilities.
The judge said that since, as the manager of a public place, it is most likely to understand the actual situation of the whole place, foresee the possible danger and damage, so that it is most likely to take the necessary measures to prevent the occurrence of losses or the extent of the damage, and to avoid and mitigate the lowest cost of the damage, so the law stipulates that it undertakes the corresponding protection obligations to engage in social activities.
In the present case, the school's obligation of safety and security should be compatible with the social activities it engages in, in particular, the basic security measures should be taken and the obligation to inform the hidden danger of concealment.
In judicial practice, it is also not advisable to impose excessive safety and security obligations on managers in public places.
If the school has set up a protective network and fulfilled the obligation to inform, it can be determined that the school is not at fault and should not bear legal responsibilities.
In addition, in the case of third-party infringement, even if the administrators of public places such as schools do not fulfill their safety and security obligations, their responsibilities are as a supplement to damages, according to the newly promulgated civil code, the administrator can also recover from the third party after assuming supplementary responsibilities.
Therefore, in such accidents, the victim should no longer extend the scope of the claim after compensation has been received from the direct infringer.
Under the normalization of epidemic prevention and control, people's enthusiasm for sports and fitness is high.
With the gradual liberalization of inter-provincial tourism business, the tourism market is about to recover.
Fujian Province has resumed inter-provincial tourism business since July 21, and on the first weekend after the opening, Xiamen, a popular tourist destination, has ushered in a peak in passenger flow.
As a popular tourist city, there are a lot of tourists who arrive in Xiamen on the weekend.
Xiamen railway station is expected to send 3.7 million passengers, and the passenger flow of the airport is dominated by students, tourism and family visits.
The tourism market has gradually recovered, and in July, Xiamen airport operated 440 flights per day, and domestic flights have returned to 80% before the epidemic.
The airline encrypted the air express lines from Xiamen to major cities such as Shanghai, Beijing, Kunming and Xi'an to seize the recovered tourism market.
At present, a number of travel agencies in Xiamen have successively launched a number of summer domestic cross-provincial tour products, and the team's itinerary is mainly based on outdoor attractions.
In view of the summer passenger peaks that appear in railway stations and airports, the relevant units have increased the number of personnel in the areas where people are easy to gather such as check-in counters and security inspection lanes, and Fujian has also optimized and upgraded the "Eight Min health code" to realize the sharing and mutual recognition of health data with 31 provinces and promote the orderly recovery of the tourism market.
Liu Dehua Liu Qingyun can "disassemble" a new spark - Xinhua
"Experimentation 2" recently announced that it will be released on December 24, becoming the first film in the New Year.
The second part is still Qiu Litao's director, Liu Dehua supervised and starring, with a completely new story.
It is reported that the addition of the "nuclear bomb" element in the second part has also made the challenges faced by the detonation experts more difficult, and a number of shocking glances in the preview have been engulfed in the first line, and the mushroom cloud of the explosion, which was engulfed by the ignition of the airport, the scene is quite shocking.
Three years ago, "bomb disposal experts" produced by the original class, won the year's May 1st box office champion, and won seven nominations at the Hong Kong Film Awards, Qiu Litao × Liu Dehua has also become in the minds of the audience's gold medal partner.
The "bomb disposal expert 2" also makes people once again look forward to whether the ace combination can wipe out a new spark.
"Bulchbreaking Experts 2" tells a completely new story: former bomb disposal expert Pan Junfeng (Liu Dehua) fainted at the scene of the explosion and was listed as a suspect by the police.
In order to find the truth, he had to turn to Dong Zhuowen (Liu Qingyun), a good friend who is also a bomb disposal expert.
The female inspector who is eager to solve the case, and at the same time Pang Ling (Nini), the ex-girlfriend of Pang Jingfeng, is also involved in it.
It is still a bomb disposal expert, but it can be felt the complexity of Liu Dehua's new role from the filing notice: he broke a leg, put on a prosthetic limb, while being chased by Liu Qingyun, who is also a bomb disposal expert, and at the same time he was commanded by his ex-girlfriend Nini.
What is the relationship between the three people, what Liu Dehua has done at the Xiangdao Hotel, and what kind of cases have been involved in the case, and what setbacks he has experienced in the career of the bomb disposal expert, all kinds of mysteries are curious.
It is understood that the highlights of the film are the world's landmark buildings in Hong Kong, coupled with the top special effects production team, to bring shocking and realistic visual impact.
(Reporter's Nie Qing)
Comprehensive Russian satellite network reported that July 26th is the Russian Navy Day, the main military parade to celebrate Navy Day was held in St. Petersburg and Kronstadt.
The Russian president and supreme commander of the armed forces of the Russian Federal Armed Forces Vladimir Putin arrived in Kronstadt to participate in the festivities, where 15 ships and submarines were reviewed.
On July 28, 2019, local time, a grand military parade was held to celebrate the Navy Day in St. Petersburg, Russia.
According to reports, Putin congratulates naval officers and soldiers on Navy Day and sailed in small boats in small boats in the Gulf of Finland next to the ships that are about to participate in a military parade at the sea, and then reviewed the reviewing troops at the subjective podium.
Putin pointed out that the Russian Navy's fleet is equipped with the latest types of ships and special equipment, and the level of equipment is constantly improving.
Speaking at the Russian Navy Day parade, Putin said: "The Russian naval fleet is equipped with warships equipped with high-precision weapons, strategic submersible cruisers and multi-role submarines, the latest aircraft and other vehicles, unique weapons and special equipment."
On June 24, local time, Russia commemorated the 75th anniversary of the victory of the Great Patriotic War.
He also said that the Russian naval fleet will achieve unique advantages through digitalization and effective means of defense.
According to the report, the main naval parade celebrating Russian Navy Day was held in St. Petersburg and Kronstadt, with the participation of a total of 46 ships, including the frigate "Admiral Kasatonov", the large anti-submarine "Admiral Kurakov", as well as large landing ships, small missile ships, frigates, submarines and so on.
Among them, a series of ships on a static display next to St. Petersburg's Hermitage Bridge, one of the most eye-catching is the reproduction of Russia's first battleship at the beginning of the 18th century "Poltava".
In order to avoid the spread of the new coronavirus, during this year's naval parade, only local residents and invited guests will be able to enter Kronstadt.
The last Sunday in July every year is Russian Navy Day.
The founder of the Beijing Philharmonic choir has died at the age of 86.
Beijing News (Reporter Liu Jin) On July 26, the Beijing Philharmonic Choir issued an obituary, the founder of the Beijing Philharmonic Choir, a well-known Chinese conductor, a music educator, a tenured academic committee member of the Central Conservatory of Music and a professor of the Department of Conductor, who died at 13:55 on July 26, 2020, at the age of 86.
Photo courtesy of the Beijing Philharmonic Choir.
Yang Hong was born in 1934 in Nanjing, Jiangsu Province, and loves music from a young age.
In the autumn of 1951, he was the conductor of the Nanjing People's Radio chorus team, and in the autumn of 1951, he was admitted to the music department of the East China Normal University in Shanghai, where he studied and conducted by Professor Yang Jiaren and the German conductor Hizmann, and studied the cursive style and polyphony from the former Soviet expert Arzamanov.
In 1958, he taught in the music department of the Beijing Normal College of the Arts, and in 1973, he was transferred to the composing department of the Central Conservatory of Music.
He founded the Beijing Philharmonic Choir in 1983.
For more than 30 years, adhering to the purpose of “love and dedication”, he has led this choir to sing around the world, and won dozens of awards in important competitions at home and abroad.
He has conducted the performances of more than 30 symphonies and choral concerts and choirs of the central orchestra, the Central National Song and Dance Troupe, the Oriental singing troupe and the Shanghai choir, and held a number of symphony and choral concerts.
His books include "band training", choral training, "two song writings", "children's song collection" (the upper and lower books), and the thesis "on the chorus sound level layout", as well as the translation of "choral choir arrangement method" and "the harmonies language of De Poussi".
Zhongxin Network Chongqing, July 26 (Reporter Liu Xian) The Chongqing Municipal Development and Reform Commission issued a message on the 26th that the city has so far withdrawn 4,404 fishermen, accounting for 42.54% of all fishermen.
The 53-year-old said in an interview with the Sino-Singapore network reporter that his grandparents fished in the Longxi River at the age of 11, followed his father's fishing at the age of 11, rocked a small boat, walked along the Longxi River, went up to Chongqing Liang Ping, went down to a long life, every time he left the house for ten days and a half months, relying on fishing to maintain his family's life.
However, since 1997, with the gradual influx of the rural population into the town, more and more and more residents in the town, the resulting environmental pollution has become more and more serious.
Paper mills, chemical plants and farms have been built along the Longxi River, which has also polluted the river's water.
By 2007 and 2008, the Longxi River had become a stinking ditch.
“The fish scales that are caught are all black, and they are also black inside when they are cut open.”
Li Daiguo said it is becoming more and more difficult to fish after river pollution.
The local government has begun to make great efforts to deal with the pollution of the Longxi River, including the dredging, river patrolling, and the management and protection of aquatic resources.
Li Daiguo also retreated from the fishermen and became a member of the river patrol team to take care of aquatic resources.
Since January 1, 2020, the Chongqing Aquatic Biological Reserve and the relevant waters of the main urban area have been completely banned.
According to the data of the Chongqing Municipal Development and Reform Commission, as of now, the city of Chongqing has accumulatively recaptured 3,403 fishing vessels and 4,643 fishing vessels that have signed a withdrawal agreement, accounting for 63.3% and 86.3% of the total three-year tasks respectively.
There have been 4,404 recaptured fishermen, accounting for 42.54% of all fishermen involved.
Of the 4,404 people who have been recaptured, 4,267 have achieved employment, accounting for 96.89% of the fishermen who have been recaptured.
The old-age insurance coverage covers 2,691 people, accounting for 61.10% of the returning fishermen.
In the next step, the city of Chongqing will carry out various special rectification actions, accelerate the clean-up and remediation of the Yangtze River trunk shoreline utilization project, complete a new round of the Yangtze River into the river, and carry out corresponding remediation actions, basically complete the rectification task of "three phosphorus, phosphorus chemical and phosphorus gypsum reservoirs), small hydropower clean-up and rectification work, promote the afforestation on both sides of the Yangt River, strengthen the construction of green mines.
Israel strengthens the prevention and control of the repeated epidemic
2020-07-26 04:56:44 Source: Guangming Daily Author:Wang Sishuo Responsibility Editor:Wang Sishuo
Israel strengthens repeated prevention and control of the epidemic
At the beginning of the new crown pneumonia epidemic, Israel's prevention and control measures have achieved remarkable results.
However, with the gradual release of prevention and control measures, the number of confirmed cases of new crown pneumonia in Israel has recently increased significantly, and the Israeli government has repeatedly taken emergency measures to strengthen the prevention and control of the epidemic.
On February 28, the first case of new crown pneumonia was confirmed in mainland Israel to quickly close all ports of entry and exit, the suspension of non-essential industries, the transformation of schools into online classes, the restriction of public transportation and non-essential social activities, the closure of cities with serious epidemics, and the joint prevention and control of military and police measures.
This series of measures quickly achieved positive results, and by mid-May in mid-May, the number of new confirmed cases of new crown pneumonia in Israel fell back to single digits.
With the control of the epidemic, Israel's various prevention and control measures have been completely unsealed, and the number of newly confirmed cases of new crown pneumonia has gradually rebounded since June.
Especially after entering July, the spread of the epidemic continues to accelerate.
In the past few days, there have been more than 1,500 new cases per day in Israel, and as of July 25, there were 916 new cases on that day.
As of July 25, there have been 59,745 confirmed cases and 448 deaths in Israel.
In the face of the rapid rebound of the epidemic, the Israeli government has repeatedly taken emergency measures to strengthen the prevention and control of the epidemic.
On July 6, after the number of confirmed cases exceeded 30,000, the Israeli government closed public entertainment venues such as gyms, swimming pools, bars and nightclubs, and introduced a policy to restrict public transportation, stipulating that the maximum number of passengers on each bus should not exceed 20.
On the 17th, the Israeli government announced a series of new restrictive measures, including the implementation of the "closed city" over the weekend, providing for the implementation of the "closed city" from 17:00 every Friday to 5 o'clock every Sunday.
During this period, people can go out, but shops, shopping malls, barbershops, beauty salons, libraries, zoos, museums, exhibition halls, swimming pools and tourist attractions will be closed, while basic services such as supermarkets and pharmacies will remain open.
At the same time, gatherings of more than 10 people are prohibited on all dates and times, gyms, studios and other places will be closed, restaurants and cafes will be banned from eating, and only take-away services will be allowed.
At the same time, the Israeli people did not pay enough attention to the severity of the epidemic and failed to join forces with the government in fighting the epidemic.
In the wake of Israel’s repeated epidemics, many people took to the streets to protest because the government's prevention and control measures affected their own economic interests.
On July 11, tens of thousands of people held a demonstration in Tel Aviv to believe that the anti-epidemic policy will affect the economy.
On the evening of the 21st, thousands of protesters gathered in front of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's official residence in Jerusalem to protest Prime Minister Netanyahu's failure to give corresponding compensation for the prevention and control measures such as banning restaurants and cafes.
In addition, many people did not comply with the provisions of wearing masks and maintaining a safe social distance of two meters during outdoor activities, in order to avoid being fined by the police because they did not wear masks, many people only wore masks on their chins or hung on their wrists.
During the repeated period of the epidemic, the school was the hardest-hit area for the spread of the new coronavirus, and according to the reporter's recent visit to the kindergarten, the kindergarten teachers and students did not wear masks according to the government's requirements, and did not maintain a safe social distance of two meters from each other, laying a hidden danger for a large number of teachers and students infected with the virus.
Professor Elie Wackersman, a member of Israel's National Security Council's expert advisory panel on the fight against the epidemic, believes that Israel is moving towards a "dangerous situation", pointing out that Israel's current epidemic prevention and control measures are not enough, and all leisure and entertainment venues and summer schools should be closed in order to control the further spread of the epidemic.
Wackersmann said that Israel lacks an overall plan to fight the epidemic, and parliament and government departments should abandon their respective interests as soon as possible, reach an agreement on the fight against the epidemic, and formulate clear steps including relevant restrictive measures in different departments.
Tel Aviv, July 25 (Xinhua) -- This newspaper's correspondent in Tel Aviv.
Ningxia Guyuan farmer Wu Fengfang but his wife Dai Tianfu, two people sitting in the car, from the home of 20 miles away, rushed to the Liangyun cultural compound.
In spite of the inconvenient legs in the past two years, the 77-year-old Dai Tianfu is still looking forward to "coming here after three forks and five times, playing tricks."
This is an inconspicuous courtyard in the original prefecture district of Guyuan City, different from the general farmhouse, the yard is often melodious Qin cavity, as well as wonderful shadow puppets, embroidery works, the traditional Qin cavity, eyebrow drama and so on.
The owner of the compound was Liang Yun, who had been a carpenter.
More than 10 years ago, he began to plan the construction of a cultural compound.
With the Liangyun cultural compound, the cultural life of the villagers has become rich and colorful.
The reporter has not yet walked into the Liangyun Cultural Commissary, and the Qin cavity of the tune has already passed out.
It is neighboring villager Bai Lixiang who is singing the Qin cavity for the villagers.
She has loved Qin cavity as a child, and now she has a small reputation in the local area, as long as she has free time, she will come to the cultural compound to perform programs for the villagers.
More recently, Percy has also played a live webcast.
Bai Lixiang said, "It's a very happy thing to have a stage for more people to see their performances."
On the stage, the performer takes a look at the board, and the player sings a tune, although he is an amateur, but his enthusiasm has not diminished.
Just like the pristine style of the farmyard, outside the Qin cavity, the "grassroots" art and non-heritage culture in the Liangyun Cultural Commissary come to the surface.
The compound has also collected more than 300 physical objects such as agricultural utensils from different eras, traditional and hand-made tiles, paper cuttings, embroidery, and shadow.
Liang Yun led the reporter to enter the exhibition hall in the courtyard, which showed his collection of old objects, old wine pots, three-strings, spinning wheels and so on.
Why did an ordinary farmer set up a cultural compound?
â€œThe shadow play is my family handiwork, and I've been studying it since I was 15 years old."
Founded in 2012, the Liangyun Cultural Institute has become the first rural "intangible cultural heritage exhibition hall" in Ningxia and a demonstration compound for the protection of intangible cultural heritage in Guyuan City.
In addition to the Liangyun Cultural Comed, more than 120 cultural courtyards and 79 non-governmental performance groups have sprouted, including more than 50 cultural courtyards on a certain scale, such as Shenjiahe Cultural Commemoration, Wang Yonghong Cultural Commemoration and Yanglang Cultural Commemoration, covering all townships and streets in the former prefecture, with more than 5,000 participants.
These grass-roots artists are active in the fields, enriching the cultural life of the masses and satisfying their spiritual needs.
“As life gets better, traditional culture can’t just fall.”
"Liu's spy war drama" once again returned "the chance of victory" to see Liu Yunlong Li Qun's opponent's "snapping drama"-Xinhua network
The 40-episode spy drama "Wonder" will land on Beijing Satellite TV on July 16.
Based on the real historical facts, it is based on Soviet military archives that have existed for the first time for many years.
Liu Yunlong, an actor known to the audience as the "spy war drama", broke through the image in the play and challenged a happy "stuttering agent".
In recent years, the popularity of dramas such as "pretender", "mask" and " kite" has proved that spy-type dramas have a strong vitality.
Different from the previous spy warfare works, "Possurrected" looked at the world and extended the story to the battlefield in the Far East of the Soviet Union.
In the context of the final stage of the anti-Japanese war in 1944, it tells the story of Tang Fei (Liu Yunlong), the secret intelligence staff of the Communist Party of China (Liu Yunlong), under the leadership of the secretary of the Chinese underground party Linhe Province and the head of the Far Eastern Intelligence Bureau of the Soviet Far Eastern Intelligence Agency.
In a lot of spy dramas, as a high-level spy, an appearance is the perfect image of handsomeness, high IQ and maturity.
However, in Liu Yunlong's view, such a person is not suitable as a spy, "spies should be the kind of people who can't be found at all, if the appearance is a very handsome image, I want everyone to pay attention to you, you can still lurk in the kite" There is a line: "If you don't come to arrest me, I will forget that I am a Kuomintang."
Therefore, Liu Yunlong ingeniously designed Tang Fei, the protagonist he played, as a "stuttering agent" with joy.
On the other side of "Proposal of Victory", Fukuhara, played by Fukuhara and Li Li Qun played by Fukuhara and Li Liqun, were supported together.
One south and one north, the two powerful drama bones, add a lot to the whole drama.
Director Yin Fei used the word "drama" to describe Li Liqun and Liu Yunlong's opponent's play in the play, "absolutely, the two of them have a special tacit understanding, and this tacit understanding of their bodies is very impactful to me.
When the actors are in the role and ensure the status of their characters, they can not only shape the characters from the perspective of the characters, but also bring more viewing possibilities to the audience.
In the play, you can also see a lot of familiar faces in the "Liu spy war drama", "Kiteflies" in the famous shock, the mighty style of the "mountain city F4", also gathered the three in the "opportunity".
He has played Song Xiao'an and Zhao Jianzhi's Hou and Liu Mingyang, and this time he once again played Tang Fei's right arm.
Director Yin Fei said, "These two people do not have inferiority, they are only in that era, in that environment with the flow."
Liu Yunlong also proposed, "We want to have a human touch. This human touch means that the people around me must have the good and the bad are the enemy, but we must also develop them, and our team will grow."
The ending of these two people in the play has also been carefully designed by Liu Yunlong, and he believes that he will give the audience a satisfactory answer.
(Reporter Qiu Wei)
Inner Mongolia Arong flag 4 students drowned official: the incident sounded the alarm
On the evening of July 25 (Reporter Li Aiping) On the evening of the 25th, the reporter learned from the Arong flag government in Hulunbuir City, Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region, that four local students died due to drowning.
At 15:50 on July 24, the Arongqi Public Security Bureau 110 received a report that six local junior high school students had drowned.
After receiving the police, the local police rushed to the scene for the first time, rescuing 2 students on the spot, and then the local emergency bureau, the water conservancy bureau and other units rushed to the scene to participate in the rescue.
According to reports, more than 80 public security police, police, fire protection, and medical care were dispatched at the rescue site, sending three rubber dinghys to continuously salvage the surrounding waters, and hired a professional rescue team to arrive at the scene to carry out underwater search through sonar detection.
The reporter learned that the local rescuers found the first killed student at 6:40 on the 25th, found the second student who was killed at 11:30 on the 25th, found the third student who was killed at 12:40 on the 25th, the last student was found at 13:34 on the 25th, the above 4 people were salvaged, and there were no vital signs identified by the local 120 emergency centers.
The official said that the drowning incident was a wake-up call for the entire society.
At present, the relevant departments of the local government are sorting out some knowledge to prevent drowning, hoping that the tragedy will not happen again.
HONG KONG, July 25 (Xinhua) -- Hong Kong's Financial Affairs and Treasury Secretary Xu Zhengyu said that Hong Kong's financial markets remain active and operating in an orderly manner.
He expressed optimism about Hong Kong's financial stability and economy.
Xu Zhengyu said at an online seminar co-organized by the Hong Kong Economic and Trade Office in Toronto and the Hong Kong-Canada Chamber of Commerce on the 24th (Toron Toronto time) that Hong Kong is experiencing a difficult situation because of the "reform storm" and the new crown pneumonia epidemic.
The Hong Kong dollar exchange rate is stabilised and skewed towards a strong exchange guarantee level.
The banking system shows no clear signs of outflows; instead, more than $11 billion has flowed in since June.
The total amount of bank deposits has also continued to increase in the past few months, and the stock market has a series of public investment fund-raising activities, and market transactions have often risen.
Xu Zhengyu said that the new crown pneumonia epidemic has put pressure on the global economy and financial markets, but the basic advantages of Hong Kong remain unchanged.
Hong Kong’s many advantages, including geography, rule of law, high-speed communication, the free flow of information and capital, and a simple and low-tax system, have continued to be a leading international financial centre.
Xu Zhengyu pointed out that the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region government has set aside HK$6 billion in the "Anti-epidemic and Anti-epidemic Fund" to create about 30,000 time-limited positions in the public and private sectors in the next two years, covering people with different skills and academic qualifications.
In order to support the development of financial technology, the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region Government has also launched the Thousand Talents Program to fund local fintech companies, start-ups and other fintech-related businesses in order to create 1,000 new jobs, employ local talent and enrich Hong Kong’s Fintech talent pool.
Looking to the future, Xu expressed optimism about Hong Kong's financial stability and economy.
He encouraged Canadian companies to take full advantage of Hong Kong’s strengths and their status as an international financial centre, an international asset and wealth management centre, and a global offshore RMB business hub to develop and invest in the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area and beyond.
"The Lancet" article praised China's anti-epidemic efforts to encourage countries to learn from the experience
As a country with a population of 1.4 billion and a similar scale in Europe or the United States, the new crown epidemic has been effectively controlled at this stage, and there has been no large-scale transmission, which has largely controlled the epidemic at home.
For more than a decade or so, China has invested heavily in domestic research and public health construction, which has made China’s preparations for the new crown much better than the severe acute respiratory syndrome (SARS).
According to the authors, when the SARS outbreak occurred in 2002, China was initially ill-prepared, especially if the pathogen could not be determined.
When the new coronavirus was discovered in December 2019, Chinese scientists would soon be able to identify the virus species, sharing genomic sequencing data with the world on January 11, 2020.
By the end of January, doctors from mainland China and Hong Kong clarified the clinical characteristics of the virus, warning the world of the threat of the new coronavirus through a research paper published in The Lancet.
China has also always been at the forefront of vaccine research, under a national state of emergency, through close domestic cooperation, such research is carried out very quickly and rigorously, and in May and July, the results of the early trials of the new crown vaccine developed in China were announced in the Lancet.
China's experience shows that it is very important to invest in national health and research systems to effectively improve laboratory capabilities.
This is the basis for a rapid and effective national response to health emergencies and global health security.
Other countries, especially in low- and middle-income countries, are well worth learning.
In addition, China's experience proves that on the basis of strong research, there must be a strong high-level and decisive scientific basis to make the correct decision, so that the new crown epidemic can be effectively controlled.
Governments and their leaders must respect science, understand its values, and take action against it in the way that is most beneficial to society.
In the early stage of the outbreak, the Chinese National Health Construction sent three groups of infectious disease experts to Wuhan to investigate the risk and spread of the new coronavirus, and their proposal provided a basis for the decision to "open the city" in Wuhan on January 23; when some experts put forward the necessity and urgency of the construction of the cabin hospital, the government quickly made a decision and quickly implemented it; at the same time, the extensive participation of the community and the masses also led to the rapid and effective control of the epidemic.
In response to a global health emergency, countries need to strengthen global cooperation and a joint response.
Journalist Yang Hong
Inner Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region Wuhai Municipal Party Committee of the former inspector white sea was expelled from the party
Recently, with the approval of the Party Committee of the Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region, with the approval of the Party Committee of the Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region, the Supervision Committee of the Discipline Inspection Commission of the Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region conducted a case review and investigation on the serious violations of discipline by the former inspector of the Wuhai Municipal Party Committee.
According to the investigation, as a leading cadre of party members and party members, the loss of ideals and beliefs, openly violating the principle of party nature for their own self-interest, against inspection and rectification; the organizational concept is indifferent, illegal arrangements for others to transfer work and accept other people's property in the selection and appointment of cadres; economic greed, illegal business enterprises to obtain huge benefits, engage in power and money transactions, with power for personal gain; life corruption, causing adverse effects.
Platinum Sea has seriously violated political discipline, organizational discipline, integrity discipline, and life discipline, which constitutes a job violation and is suspected of bribery crimes and embezzlement crimes, and it does not converge after the 18th National Congress of the Communist Party of China.
In accordance with the relevant provisions of the "Regulations on Disciplinary Disciplinary Disciplinary Affairs of the Communist Party of China" and the Supervision Law of the People's Republic of China, after the meeting of the Standing Committee of the Discipline Commission of the Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region reviewed and reported to the Party Committee of the Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region for approval, it was decided to give Platinum Hai expulsion from the Party and adjust its treatment according to the provisions; collected his disciplinary and illegal income; transferred his suspected crimes to the procuratorial organs for review and prosecution.
On the afternoon of the evening of the 25th local time, a small plane crashed into the top floor of a multi-storey residential building in Wessel County of North Rhine-Westphalia in Germany, killing a total of three people in the accident.
In a joint statement issued that evening, the Duisburg Prefecture Prosecution Service, the Wessel County Police Department and the Wessel City Fire Department said that at about 14:40 that day, two small airplanes crashed into a home on the penthouse of a multi-storey residential building on Whisper Camp Street in Wessel County, killing three people.
On the same day, it took off from the city of Marr in Ruhr district of North Rhine-Westphalia, took off again after docking at the airport in Wessel County, and then crashed into the residential building.
The victim may have been a female householder and two passengers on a small aircraft in the house that had been hit.
A two-year-old child in the room suffered only minor injuries and was safely rescued.
The remaining occupants of the house were not injured in the accident, but the mood has not calmed down.
The scene screen reported by the German news agency shows that the houses affected by the accident at one time were billowing with thick smoke, and the firefighters could see that the house was severely damaged after extinguishing the fire.
At present, the cause of the plane crash is not clear.
The Rheinische Post quoted the police as saying that there were clues that the plane had disintegrated before it crashed into a residential building.
According to the police, multiple parts of the crashed aircraft were found at the scene of the accident.
The German criminal police are working with the Duisburg prosecution and the German Federal Aviation Accident Investigation Agency to investigate the cause of the accident.
On the same day, the reporter learned from the Chinese Consulate General in Düsseldorf that the museum got in touch with the local police and fire departments, according to the judgment at the scene, there were no Chinese citizens among the casualties.
The Ministry of Health of Singapore announced on the 26th that as of 12 o'clock on the same day, there were 481 new crown confirmed cases in Singapore, with a total of 50,369 confirmed cases and 27 cumulative deaths.
According to the data, of the newly confirmed cases, 5 are local community cases, 4 are imported cases, and the rest are foreign workers living in dedicated dormitories.
Singapore’s health ministry said 98% of the new confirmed cases were related to known infections.
There are still 173 newly crowned patients being treated in the hospital, most of whom are in stable or improved condition and no one is in intensive care units.
In addition, 4,648 people were segregated at community facilities.
Foreign workers account for the vast majority of new coronavirus-infected people in Singapore.
According to statistics, there are 200,000 foreign workers living in 43 dormitories for foreign workers, and there are about 100,000 foreign workers living in dormitories of other types.
Singapore's anti-epidemic interdepartmental working group recently said that the Singapore government is speeding up the testing of the last foreign workers with a high infection rate.
The vast majority of foreign workers will be able to return to work after the testing of all dedicated dormitories has been completed, but they still have to undergo regular new crown tests.
Dapeng director's auspicious wishes shortlisted for the Golden Knight Award - Xinhua.com
On July 18, the twenty-third Shanghai International Film Festival announced the official list of selected films.
Dappeng's director's first reality-themed film "auspicious" was successfully shortlisted for this year's Golden Knight Award, while the film officially released the first poster.
Poster Fragment
"Auspicious" is Daphragm director's first real-life theme work, and it is also his second relationship with the Golden Knight Award.
The film tells such a story: a comedy film director suddenly imagines to return to his hometown in the northeastern countryside, hoping to make a literary and artistic film about how the family will make the New Year, resulting in a series of accidents.
The members of the family who gathered because of the film, completed the final meeting.
In today's release of the film poster, a member of the family - "three uncles" Wang auspicious sitting in the middle of the picture smoking a cigarette, the background is covered with silver in the northeastern black land, the foreground is the red lantern that the Chinese must hang every New Year.
The red lantern, which symbolizes festivities and reunions, has formed a huge contrast with Wang auspicion, and seems to reveal the complexity and entanglement in this family relationship.
It is reported that in the film, in addition to the "three uncles" Wang's auspicious daughter played by actor Liu Lu, the rest of the scenes are completed by the real director's family, the film's experimental audio-visual style, breaking the boundaries of drama and reality, to bring the audience a new immersive viewing experience.
According to the director Dapeng, "auspicious" creation is derived from "ancient intention", during the shooting of a series of sudden changes in the family, so that the original shooting plan had to be changed, there is no script's life was finally recorded into a film, but released beyond the tension of the design.
Director Dapeng how to deal with this "God's will", and how to continue to meet the various changes brought about by God's will?
Undoubtedly "auspicious" is full of experimental, almost all amateur lineup and innovative audio-visual style will turn the life in front of the camera into a movie, under the package of real images, the audience will also find the shadow of themselves and his family from the family presented in the film, with the end of the family gathering in the film, arousing a series of thoughts.
