Chen Maobo pointed out that Hong Kong's economy has been hit again due to the outbreak of the epidemic, calling on all walks of life
HONG KONG, July 26 (Xinhua) -- Financial Secretary of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Hong Kong Special Administrative Region Government, Chen Maobo, said on the 26th that Hong Kong's response to the impact of a new wave of new crown pneumococcal pneumonia has also been affected by business exchanges and economic activities, which have shown signs of reviving.
The Hong Kong Special Administrative Hong Kong Special Administrative Region Government once again calls on large and medium-sized owners to reduce their rents and spend a difficult time with retail households, restaurants and small and medium-sized enterprises.
On the same day, Chen Maobo published an article on the Internet entitled "The road to a rough recovery".
He said that the number of recent confirmed cases of new crown pneumonia in Hong Kong is high, and the situation is grim, which has affected people's livelihood and plagued the economy.
When the epidemic is repeated, it is mainly necessary to strictly prevent imported cases, and to deal with and interrupt the chain of transmission of the virus as soon as possible; when the epidemic is under control, it should resume economic activities accordingly in a timely and appropriate manner.
He pointed out that in the face of the impact of the new wave of the epidemic, the business exchanges and economic activities that had already shown signs of recovery have also been affected.
For the business community, in addition to the spirit of the contract, social responsibility is equally important, especially those groups that receive large subsidies from the government in the "guaranteed employment plan".
Hong Kong’s economic conditions are still very strong in the second quarter of this year, but the pace of contraction seems to have eased slightly.
In terms of exports, he believes that the external situation in Hong Kong is still serious.
Hong Kong's development in the past few decades has shown that every crisis hides new opportunities, and every difficulty hides the key to future development.
The largest earthquake in the eastern waters of Taiwan this year
TAIPEI, July 26 (Xinhua) -- A 6.1-magnitude earthquake on the Richter scale occurred at 20:52 in Taiwan's eastern waters on the 26th, with a maximum magnitude of 4-magnitude, which is the largest earthquake in Taiwan this year.
According to Taiwanese media reports such as the Comprehensive Central News Agency, the China Times Electronic News and the ETtoday News Cloud, Taiwan's meteorological department reported that the epicenter of the earthquake was 86.5 kilometers southeast of the Yilan county government, that is, the eastern sea area of Taiwan, with a depth depth of 53 kilometers.
The Chinese earthquake network measured the earthquake at a magnitude of 5.5.
The largest tremors in various parts of Taiwan are: Hualien county level 4, Yilan County, Taitung County, Nantou County, Yunlin County 3 level, and other counties and cities measured 1 to 2 earthquakes.
Taiwan's meteorological department pointed out that the earthquake is the largest in Taiwan this year this year, which belongs to the occult belt-type earthquake at the intersection of the plate, and its epicenter has often experienced earthquakes in the past, and it has also been relatively active this year.
In the next week, it is still not ruled out that there will be aftershocks of more than magnitude 4.
